# Copy to agent/.env on the machine (gitignored).
# This machine's name (OpenTelemetry host.name) is detected: on GCP the VM's instance name (renaming the VM shows on the
# dashboards within a minute), elsewhere the OS hostname. It is the card name on Fleet Overview, metrics `instance` /
# `host_name`, traces / logs host.name, and the key of thresholds and the machine inventory. Set HOST_NAME only where
# detection gives a useless name (this Mac: the agent's container hostname). Unrelated to the certificate's name.
# HOST_NAME=
# The project this machine belongs to (OpenTelemetry service.namespace): `service_namespace` label on its metrics
# (Fleet Overview's filter), and the namespace of apps here that do not set their own (= their OpenObserve stream).
SERVICE_NAMESPACE=sclaser_food
# The collector's gateway: <ip or name>:4317 (the collector's own agent: 127.0.0.1:4317). Must be one of the names/IPs in
# the gateway certificate (docs/collector-runbook.md step 3).
GATEWAY_ENDPOINT=34.0.0.1:4317
# Client certificate directory (ca.crt, client.crt, client.key: key + CSR made here, signed by the collector;
# docs/agent-runbook.md step 1). Local mode only: ../pki/clients/<machine> from scripts/pki.sh client.
# AGENT_CERTS_DIR=./certs
# Linux VM: also run node_exporter from this compose file. Remove the line if the VM already runs one (then set
# NODE_EXPORTER_TARGET to its address, default 127.0.0.1:9100).
COMPOSE_PROFILES=node-exporter
# Where apps send OTLP: 127.0.0.1:4318 for apps on the host; for apps in Docker containers the docker0 address
# (ip -4 addr show docker0, usually 172.17.0.1:4318), which they reach as host.docker.internal with extra_hosts host-gateway.
# AGENT_OTLP_BIND=127.0.0.1:4318
